      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T08:06:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is generally very bad practice to just take a random context and assume you can reuse it. This context may be removed (here you leak it), or it might change.\n\nAt the very least you need a very clear explanation of why all contexts are equivalent for this.\n...and by the way I don\u0027t think they are – this is going to vary per user right ?\n\nIf data saver is per-user, then you\u0027re using the wrong context and you\u0027re getting the wrong value.\n\nAlso, you probably want to take the application context out of the context if it\u0027s not already an application context, to avoid leaks.",
